# FewerTrips19 (2026-10-16, config E = config D + this patch): STRATA_D19_HOIST=1. In the EXL3 slim doorbell graph the shared-expert combine and the resident experts' kernel B
# (exl3_moe_coop B, bo as its shared term) used to run AFTER the wait for the host's CPU rows although they do not depend on them. With the knob they are captured BEFORE the wait; only the add of the
# host-reduced rows (add_inplace + zero of the mirror) stays after it, so the y-push -> next-ring chain is shorter (HS_TRACE wait-for-ring 0.317 -> 0.282 ms per ring). Same arithmetic,
# the fp32 association of bo changes ((shared + resident) + cpu instead of (shared + cpu) + resident), the same class as every slot-count change.
# Also STRATA_D19_SKIPCOLD=1 (RESEARCH, LOSSY, off, not in config E): the cold experts are not computed (rows zero): the quality probe of a card-only pass (top-1 92.3% vs the exact model).
# Measured (ABBA, 29 realistic prompts + 12 probes, fresh restart per arm): decode 29.81 (D) -> 30.94 tok/s (+3.8%, paired 24/29 faster), probes 26.27 -> 26.47, TTFT unchanged (20.2 s).
# Base: Strata v0.1.41 (fb58e0dbc839) + patches/strata/0001..0020, applied in order with `git apply -p1`.

